# Scacelith - Hrvatski
#
# Translation of assets/i18n/en.lang (same keys, same {n}). Plurals have three forms:
# one (1, 21, 31...)|few (2-4, 22-24...)|other (0, 5-20, 25-30...).
# Register: formal "vi" (lower case mid-sentence), as Croatian software; buttons and menu commands
# use the short command form ("Spremi", "Odustani", "Ponudi remi"); sentence case, never Title Case.
# Titles are in capitals (the title face is an inscriptional capital face).
# The player's gender is unknown: no adjective or past participle that agrees with the player where
# a neutral wording exists ("Pobjeda" for "You won", "Kodovi su spremljeni" for "I saved them").
# Standard Croatian chess terms (Hrvatski šahovski savez): kralj, dama, top, lovac, skakač, pješak;
# zapisnik (scoresheet), tempo igre (time control), rejting (rating), remi, predaja, nepravilan potez.
# Keep the sections: other parts of the game add their keys in sections of their own.

